WEBVTT

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:37.780
<b>#6 First Race!</b>

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:34.820
Excuse us.

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.780
Is the manager around?

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:40.740
Yeah, welcome.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:44.090
Oh, it's you girls. Good timing.

00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:46.410
I just finished.

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:49.500
Wow!

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:53.270
Tomo-chan and Fuyune-chan, 
your bikes are so shiny.

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:54.520
Of course they are.

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:56.970
I gave them both a tune-up and polished them.

00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:00.100
This one's Akizuki-chan's road racer.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:03.670
Not only is it affordable,
but it's good for touring, commuting,

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:06.360
and even a bit of racing.

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:08.360
It's a perfect first bike.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.780
Wow. You picked a good one, Tomo-chan.

00:02:12.910 --> 00:02:17.570
It may be affordable, but I 
spent all my savings on it.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:19.950
I'll have to help around my 
family's shop for a while.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:21.700
What does your family do?

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:24.810
We run a liquor store called Benten Liquors.

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:28.620
My family pays me a little bit of an 
allowance for helping out around the store.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:31.330
Benten Liquors? That's where we get our sake.

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:32.470
Really?

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:36.520
Yeah, most of the stuff my family 
buys comes from your store.

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:39.220
Really? So you're one of our regulars.

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:41.460
But that must be hard.

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:43.150
In addition to schoolwork 
and club activities,

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:44.820
you even help out at your family's store.

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:45.850
Yeah.

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:49.720
But because of that, I was 
able to buy this bike.

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:51.660
It's no big deal.

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:54.060
Take good care of it.

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:55.240
Of course.

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:58.110
This is your Pinarello, Kamikura-chan.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:02.290
Just look at this beautiful 
full carbon frame.

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:06.620
The components are top grade, too.
They're electric.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:10.420
Wow, I bet it even climbs hills easily.

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:11.050
What?

00:03:11.050 --> 00:03:13.250
I see it all the time in commercials.

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:17.610
Because of the motor, you can 
quickly speed up any hill.

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:19.880
That's not the same thing, Maiharu-chan.

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:22.930
Only the gear shift on 
this bicycle is electric.

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:25.800
It doesn't help you move forward at all.

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:29.650
It's totally different from pedelec bikes.

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:31.400
What? Really?

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:34.770
I heard it was really expensive,
so I just assumed...

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:37.890
It certainly was unbelievably expensive.

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:40.200
I cleaned out my savings, too.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:44.950
Besides, I won't have regrets 
later if I buy the best stuff now.

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:50.940
That's enough chat. Go test your bikes out.

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:53.220
Everyone has their own preference 
when it comes to positioning.

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:55.580
I'll adjust anything that doesn't 
feel right, so just let me know.

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:57.270
Oh, but...

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:01.260
We still don't know enough 
to have preferences.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:03.220
Then Higa-chan, why don't you go with them?

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:06.290
Since you ride a road racer,
you should be able to give them advice.

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:07.220
Okay.

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:11.260
We're off.

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:12.550
We're off.

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:14.050
See you later.

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:19.820
They're lucky they all have their own bikes.

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:22.930
What are you going to do 
about the Night Criterium?

00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:27.660
Apparently beginners can enter 
using whatever bike they want,

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:29.580
so I thought I'd ride that.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:34.540
You're going to be the only one on 
a mommy bike? You can't be serious.

00:04:36.110 --> 00:04:37.980
You're hopeless.

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:39.670
Okay, leave it to me.

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:40.500
What?

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:42.680
Who do you think I am?

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:45.970
I'm Cycle Flat's manager, Hooji Korone.

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:53.030
We're back.

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:56.560
What's going on?

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:00.070
I'm not sure either.

00:05:01.270 --> 00:05:02.440
That should do it.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:05.860
Maiharu-chan, get on.

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:12.220
Yeah, that looks about right.

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:14.390
Where did that bicycle come from?

00:05:14.390 --> 00:05:19.840
That thing? I threw together a leftover 
frame in the back and some old parts.

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:22.920
It doesn't look like much, 
but I guarantee it works.

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:26.640
How does it feel?

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:28.570
Great!

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:30.490
Manager, this bike...

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:32.300
Yeah, you can borrow it for a while.

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:32.850
What?

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:35.770
You can ride it during the Night Criterium.

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:38.520
What? Really?

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:42.790
Yeah, think of it as a freebie 
for buying two of my bikes.

00:05:42.790 --> 00:05:44.730
That's great, Hiromi.

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:47.250
Now, all four of us can ride road racers.

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:50.450
Yeah. Thank you, Manager.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:52.350
There aren't many days 
left before the criterium.

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:55.450
You should practice hard so you 
get used to riding your bikes.

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:56.960
Okay.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:00.340
Oh, right. Don't forget to wear helmets.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:27.610
<b>Kamakura
Night
Criterium</b>

00:06:27.610 --> 00:06:29.610
Thanks for waiting, everyone.

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:30.580
There.

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:32.910
They're finally here.

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:35.040
Oh! Yuika-chan, you came, too?

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:39.590
Yeah. After my sister told me they'd be 
arriving today, I couldn't sit still.

00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:43.390
Sensei, we can't wait, either.

00:06:43.390 --> 00:06:44.250
Okay, okay.

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:47.030
Ta-dah! They're fresh out of the oven.

00:06:47.030 --> 00:06:50.720
It's the Minami Kamakura Girls 
Bicycle Club team jersey.

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:13.180
The clothes really do make the woman.

00:07:13.790 --> 00:07:17.740
Hiromi, you seem confused. 
That wasn't a compliment.

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:18.310
What?

00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:22.210
But it's true that you all look great.

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:25.340
That's because your design 
was great, Yuika-chan.

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:27.390
Thank you.

00:07:27.390 --> 00:07:33.050
But don't you think these racing 
pants are too form-fitting?

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:36.810
I don't like that we can't 
wear anything under them.

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:38.100
What are you talking about?

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:41.880
Racing pants are worn on bare 
skin to prevent chafing.

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:45.600
And they're form-fitting 
to reduce wind resistance.

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:48.360
They're shaped that way for a reason.

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:50.360
Really?

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:53.860
But these colors might be a little flashy...

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:57.370
Do you not like my design?

00:07:57.370 --> 00:07:59.550
Oh, that's not what I meant.

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:03.420
I was just surprised since 
they're flashier in person.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:05.270
What's wrong with being flashy?

00:08:05.270 --> 00:08:08.430
It's like we're advertising to everyone 
that the bicycle club is here.

00:08:08.430 --> 00:08:10.040
Right, Natsumi?

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:17.220
Huh? Well, it certainly isn't a plain design,
but some cycling wear is even flashier.

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:19.340
I like them.

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:21.890
They're flashy enough to get 
you in the right mindset.

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:23.210
Mindset?

00:08:23.210 --> 00:08:28.540
Yeah, I feel like riding when 
I put my cycling wear on.

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:30.420
It's like a switch being flipped.

00:08:30.420 --> 00:08:33.130
That's it. That's it, Tomo-chan.

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:35.930
It's important for us 
to produce results today

00:08:35.930 --> 00:08:38.240
in order to be acknowledged 
as an official club, right?

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:42.750
So we should all wear these uniforms 
to get in the right mindset.

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:46.460
We can't be faint-hearted, huh?

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:53.170
You're right.

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:57.010
Thanks, Yuika. I'll race in my uniform.

00:08:57.010 --> 00:08:58.060
Okay.

00:08:58.890 --> 00:09:01.660
Let's go, everyone.

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:02.710
Yeah.

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:13.940
We come by here every day,
but it feels different tonight.

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:16.860
Yeah, it's like it's not our school.

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:18.780
Anyway...

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:23.030
We're sort of...

00:09:23.030 --> 00:09:25.460
Out of place, aren't we?

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:27.170
Pull yourselves together.

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:30.040
Don't be so timid before 
the race has even started.

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:33.250
That's right. We're supposed 
to produce results here,

00:09:33.250 --> 00:09:35.970
so my grandmother will 
recognize the bicycle club.

00:09:37.670 --> 00:09:42.120
<i>Racers, please finish registering</i>

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:46.820
<i>and attach the number plate and 
sensor you received to your bike.</i>

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:47.770
Come on. Go get registered.

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:48.890
Okay.

00:09:52.180 --> 00:09:54.200
Hey, Sis!

00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:56.120
Nagisa?

00:09:56.780 --> 00:09:59.240
What are you doing before the race?

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:01.450
And the manager?

00:10:00.140 --> 00:10:06.750
<b>Korone</b>

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:06.750
Indeed. I'm Yakisoba Flat's 
manager, Hooji Korone.

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:08.640
What are you doing?

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:12.810
It's a local bike event. 
How could I stay away?

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:16.380
Here, it's fresh. It's good.

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:22.720
It is good.

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:26.350
Right? I recommend the sardine 
and tendon omelet, too.

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:29.030
Anyway, where are the girls?

00:10:29.030 --> 00:10:30.510
They're registering.

00:10:30.510 --> 00:10:33.730
Oh, right. Who's this girl?

00:10:34.290 --> 00:10:36.190
Akizuki-san's sister.

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:38.320
Akizuki-chan's, huh?

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:40.420
Yes. My name's Yuika.

00:10:40.420 --> 00:10:42.090
Nice to meet you, Korone-chan.

00:10:42.970 --> 00:10:43.660
"Chan"?

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:46.910
Are you helping your older 
sister today? Good girl.

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:52.920
I'm not a kid!

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:55.340
We got number plates and...

00:10:55.340 --> 00:10:56.700
What is this?

00:10:56.700 --> 00:10:58.300
Apparently, it's a sensor.

00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:01.800
They use it to count laps and measure times.

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:04.380
Wow, it's so high tech.

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:08.600
Should I put my number plates on my basket?

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:11.570
It says to put the sensor on the front fork.

00:11:11.570 --> 00:11:13.310
What's the front fork?

00:11:13.310 --> 00:11:16.270
It looks like a lot of 
our classmates are here.

00:11:16.270 --> 00:11:20.280
And they're all people who don't 
seem too interested in bicycles.

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:22.170
Maybe it's because the race is at school.

00:11:22.170 --> 00:11:25.080
But it's open to the public.

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:27.930
Want me to tell you why?

00:11:29.350 --> 00:11:31.100
Azuma-senpai?

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:32.540
It's been a while.

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:35.220
What is the reason?

00:11:35.220 --> 00:11:37.960
It's because all the school's sports teams

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:41.110
agreed to participate for 
promising new members.

00:11:41.110 --> 00:11:43.830
Like what we did with you?

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:44.470
Yeah.

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:46.930
You probably haven't heard,

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:48.890
but lately the sports clubs 
have been stealing members

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:51.120
from each other with increased fervor.

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:54.440
The situation was pretty 
strained for a while.

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:56.590
But then the principal...

00:11:56.590 --> 00:12:00.030
Why don't you settle things at this event?

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:06.410
I'm sure my grandmother is enjoying this.

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:09.940
Like I said during our race,

00:12:09.940 --> 00:12:14.040
even the swim team and track team can 
participate equally in a bike race,

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:16.780
so everyone agreed to the principal's terms.

00:12:16.780 --> 00:12:18.700
Then they're...

00:12:18.700 --> 00:12:22.510
...sports club members passionate 
about acquiring new members?

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:25.790
Are you here for Natsumi-chan again?

00:12:26.590 --> 00:12:28.930
No, no. I've given up on her.

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:32.430
I'm just here because I like competition.

00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:36.150
And the sports clubs aren't 
the only ones participating.

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:39.480
The art club, the literature 
club, the woodwinds club...

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:41.610
I think that's the cosplay club.

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:43.500
Why are the cultural clubs participating?

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:45.920
Who knows? I'm not sure.

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:47.190
Regardless of the nature of the event,

00:12:47.190 --> 00:12:51.540
maybe they think it'll count toward their 
club's achievements if they stand out.

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:54.580
In other words, they're taking 
this race seriously, too.

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:59.790
Oh, right. You should be careful.

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:04.510
I did say earlier that everyone would 
be on equal footing in a bike race,

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:07.390
but there's one group that's 
different from the rest.

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:13.170
That's right. Since you're the bicycle club,
everyone's got it out for you.

00:13:13.170 --> 00:13:15.560
Anyway, good luck.

00:13:24.510 --> 00:13:26.400
Good evening, everyone.

00:13:26.710 --> 00:13:30.200
I'm Hibara Kano, and I'll 
be hosting this event.

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:31.950
Thank you for having me.

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:38.840
First, I'd like to thank Principal Kamikura 
for allowing this event to take place.

00:13:40.700 --> 00:13:42.940
The Night Criterium will take place

00:13:42.940 --> 00:13:48.590
on a one-kilometer course set up inside 
Minami Kamakura High School's campus.

00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:55.560
Riders in the beginner class will race over 
ten laps or ten kilometers of the course.

00:13:55.560 --> 00:14:00.020
The intermediate and advanced classes 
will race over 30 laps or 30 kilometers.

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:04.410
Pads have been placed at dangerous 
locations along the course,

00:14:04.410 --> 00:14:09.610
and lights have been set up along it, 
but the race will start after dark.

00:14:09.610 --> 00:14:13.330
A first aid station has also 
been set up just in case,

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:15.250
Huh? My mom's here.

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:17.650
but please be careful, 
so you won't have to use it.

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:16.040
What?

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:18.950
Is that nurse your mom?

00:14:18.950 --> 00:14:20.040
Yeah.

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:24.200
She said she had to work tonight,
so what's she doing here supporting me?

00:14:24.200 --> 00:14:27.060
I think she's working right now.

00:14:27.060 --> 00:14:30.580
Since the beginner class 
has so many participants,

00:14:30.580 --> 00:14:32.770
we'd like to change how the race will start.

00:14:32.770 --> 00:14:33.760
What?

00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:38.800
Most of the beginner class is made up
 of Minami Kamakura High students,

00:14:38.800 --> 00:14:41.340
so the race will begin in class order.

00:14:41.340 --> 00:14:42.770
The first-years will start first,

00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:49.360
<b>KAMAKURA CUP Night Criterium in Minami Kamakura High School
A Message to All Participants</b>

00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:49.360
followed by the second-years, then finally 
the third-years and general public.

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:51.750
Which means...

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:54.830
We'll be starting at the front.

00:14:56.290 --> 00:15:00.500
There's already enough pressure on us.
I can't believe we're starting at the front.

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:04.490
It's okay. We have road racers.

00:15:04.490 --> 00:15:07.880
They're stronger than mommy bikes.

00:15:07.880 --> 00:15:12.390
But I lost on a road racer to 
Azuma-senpai on a mommy bike.

00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:13.910
Well...

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:16.670
Are they okay?

00:15:16.670 --> 00:15:19.430
I should help them relax.

00:15:20.820 --> 00:15:22.900
Girls, listen up.

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:27.980
Have you heard the expression 
"all for one, one for all"?

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:30.500
That sounds familiar.

00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:32.450
Is that from <i>The Three Musketeers?</i>

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:37.330
Bike racing might seem like an 
individual competition, but it's not.

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:42.190
It's about working together with your 
teammates to reach the finish line.

00:15:42.190 --> 00:15:43.890
Working together?

00:15:44.510 --> 00:15:47.690
That's right. The four 
of you are a single unit.

00:15:47.690 --> 00:15:53.930
If everyone does what they can, 
you're sure to be strong together.

00:15:54.330 --> 00:15:57.390
But how can we work together?

00:15:57.390 --> 00:16:02.390
I'm about to tell you exactly 
how to do it, so listen up.

00:16:02.960 --> 00:16:04.850
<b>Beginner Race
Will Begin Shortly</b>

00:16:04.850 --> 00:16:08.780
It's nearly time for the 
beginner race to start.

00:16:09.410 --> 00:16:11.940
Is everyone ready?

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:15.270
I feel nervous.

00:16:15.270 --> 00:16:18.030
My throat feels tight.

00:16:18.030 --> 00:16:20.700
Well, we have to do it now. Right?

00:16:21.300 --> 00:16:21.960
Natsumi?

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:22.670
Huh?

00:16:22.670 --> 00:16:24.290
Oh, yeah. Let's do our best.

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:30.460
Anyway, I feel a little nervous about 
being chased by all these people.

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:33.470
Yeah, and we're right next to—

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:36.050
Bear! Bear, bear, bear!

00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:38.300
The race will start in ten seconds.

00:16:41.460 --> 00:16:46.650
<i>It's starting. It's really starting.</i>

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:49.100
Five seconds.

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:51.220
Four.

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:53.250
Three.

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:55.320
Two.

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:57.210
One.

00:16:59.030 --> 00:17:00.300
Start!

00:17:04.250 --> 00:17:06.980
<i>We just have to pedal as hard as we can.</i>

00:17:06.980 --> 00:17:07.830
Wait.

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:08.520
Huh?

00:17:08.520 --> 00:17:09.800
Natsumi's not coming.

00:17:09.800 --> 00:17:11.960
What? Natsumi-chan?

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:17.930
While the rest of the lead group has left, 
there's one racer who hasn't started yet.

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:21.250
She seems to be having 
trouble with her cleats.

00:17:21.250 --> 00:17:25.140
Meanwhile, the lead pack is 
approaching the first turn.

00:17:28.680 --> 00:17:32.190
Higa-san, calm down.
Just do it like you always do.

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:33.820
O-Okay...

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:34.680
It's in.

00:17:34.680 --> 00:17:37.780
The second-years are starting now.

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:42.790
<i>I'm falling.</i>

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:44.720
Natsumi-chan!

00:17:44.720 --> 00:17:49.290
<i>Someone has fallen. Someone has 
fallen at the starting line.</i>

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:49.310
Hiromi?

00:17:49.310 --> 00:17:50.290
What are you doing?

00:17:51.540 --> 00:17:53.060
Ouch.

00:17:52.170 --> 00:17:53.760
Are you okay, Natsumi-chan?

00:17:55.410 --> 00:17:56.010
Y-Yeah.

00:17:56.010 --> 00:17:58.090
Can you stand? Are you hurt anywhere?

00:17:58.090 --> 00:18:00.070
No, I'm fine.

00:18:00.070 --> 00:18:02.470
Hey, you're in the way.

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:04.170
If you're going, then go.

00:18:04.170 --> 00:18:05.700
Azuma-senpai...

00:18:05.700 --> 00:18:07.690
Maiharu-san, it's been a while.

00:18:08.500 --> 00:18:10.650
The president of the light swimming club...

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:12.150
Mikako, let's go.

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:13.650
Okay, okay.

00:18:16.830 --> 00:18:17.860
We'll be waiting for you.

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:26.170
Natsumi-chan, we should go, too.

00:18:26.170 --> 00:18:31.640
What? But you don't have 
to start over with me.

00:18:31.640 --> 00:18:34.210
Your bike seems to be okay.

00:18:34.560 --> 00:18:35.970
Let's start together.

00:18:35.970 --> 00:18:36.940
She's right.

00:18:37.670 --> 00:18:39.050
Fuyune-chan?

00:18:39.050 --> 00:18:40.640
Akizuki-san, you, too?

00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:42.570
Hiromi, here's your bike.

00:18:42.570 --> 00:18:43.690
Th-Thanks.

00:18:43.690 --> 00:18:46.350
You're borrowing it, remember? 
You can't just throw it away.

00:18:46.350 --> 00:18:48.460
I thought you two went on ahead.

00:18:48.460 --> 00:18:52.610
Do you think we're that heartless?

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:55.860
That's right. It's the 
bicycle club's first race.

00:18:55.860 --> 00:18:57.230
Let's ride together.

00:18:57.230 --> 00:18:58.860
Quit lollygagging.

00:18:58.860 --> 00:19:01.470
Let's start together again.

00:19:01.470 --> 00:19:03.070
All of you...

00:19:03.400 --> 00:19:07.780
You can do it. You can still make up for it.

00:19:07.780 --> 00:19:09.540
The race is just getting started.

00:19:11.450 --> 00:19:13.960
Everyone's cheering for us.

00:19:23.650 --> 00:19:26.430
We've got to do our best now.

00:19:26.430 --> 00:19:27.810
Exactly.

00:19:35.330 --> 00:19:37.820
Is everyone ready?

00:19:38.250 --> 00:19:39.190
Yeah.

00:19:39.190 --> 00:19:40.400
Yes.

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:42.320
I'm ready any time.

00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:47.830
Here we go.

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:40.100
<i>The appeal of road bikes on full display 
makes you want to start riding tomorrow.</i>

00:21:40.100 --> 00:21:43.160
<i>A-O-P: The first cycling club.</i>

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:48.090
<b>Choose the frame</b>

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:48.090
<b>Choose the size</b>

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:48.090
<b>Accidents (Flats)</b>

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:48.090
<b>Accidents (Chain)</b>

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:48.090
<b>Must-have items</b>

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:48.090
<b>Useful items</b>

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:48.090
<b>Maintenance</b>

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:48.090
<b>Proper posture</b>

00:21:44.440 --> 00:21:48.460
<i>In this segment, we bring you must-see 
information for newbies to road bikes with</i>

00:21:48.090 --> 00:21:53.760
<b>Fukuo Yui</b>

00:21:48.090 --> 00:21:53.760
<b>Hirose Yuki</b>

00:21:48.460 --> 00:21:50.640
<i>A-O-P's Hirose Yuki...</i>

00:21:50.640 --> 00:21:52.860
<i>And Fukuo Yui.</i>

00:21:54.550 --> 00:21:57.400
<i>"While riding a bike,
it's impossible to avoid..."</i>

00:21:58.460 --> 00:22:01.290
<i>"Uh-oh! The chain came off!"</i>

00:22:02.130 --> 00:22:03.930
<i>"Now you've done it."</i>

00:22:04.830 --> 00:22:07.130
<i>"What should I do?"</i>

00:22:07.130 --> 00:22:14.140
<b>Dealing With Accidents 2: The Bike Chain</b>

00:22:07.780 --> 00:22:09.310
<i>This time we'll learn</i>

00:22:09.310 --> 00:22:13.330
<i>techniques for fixing slipped bike 
chains that even beginners can use.</i>

00:22:14.140 --> 00:22:16.560
On a bike with this many gears,

00:22:16.560 --> 00:22:19.270
it seems like it would be difficult 
to fix a slipped bike chain.

00:22:19.270 --> 00:22:25.330
Since the bike uses a derailleur,
the chain will definitely sometimes slip.

00:22:19.270 --> 00:22:27.400
<b>Y's Road Ochanomizu
Manager Yamada Yunosuke-san</b>

00:22:24.960 --> 00:22:26.070
What?

00:22:25.330 --> 00:22:29.960
But don't worry if it does come off.

00:22:29.960 --> 00:22:33.370
It's easy to fix, so let's give it a try.

00:22:31.910 --> 00:22:33.370
Yes, please.

00:22:33.370 --> 00:22:36.290
The derailleur is attached to

00:22:36.290 --> 00:22:39.490
the back of the bike and has 
something called a tensioner.

00:22:36.290 --> 00:22:41.880
<b>Tensioner</b>

00:22:39.490 --> 00:22:41.270
The tensioner.

00:22:40.060 --> 00:22:43.940
This maintains the tension in the chain.

00:22:43.940 --> 00:22:51.020
If you push it forward, the chain sags.

00:22:45.590 --> 00:22:55.100
<b>Press the derailleur's tensioner to loosen the chain</b>

00:22:51.020 --> 00:22:52.280
You're right.

00:22:52.280 --> 00:22:58.010
Take the loose part of the chain and 
place it on the teeth of the closest gear

00:22:55.100 --> 00:23:06.280
<b>Replace the chain on the gear and slowly turn the pedals</b>

00:22:58.010 --> 00:22:59.810
and slowly turn the pedals.

00:23:01.190 --> 00:23:02.200
And then...

00:23:02.200 --> 00:23:03.250
It's working. That was quick.

00:23:03.250 --> 00:23:04.530
Wow.

00:23:04.530 --> 00:23:06.280
That's it.

00:23:06.280 --> 00:23:09.220
It's quite easy, so give it a try.

00:23:09.220 --> 00:23:10.490
Yeah, let's.

00:23:10.490 --> 00:23:14.920
If you press clean parts of the derailleur,
 you can keep your hands clean.

00:23:11.940 --> 00:23:13.450
Right here?

00:23:14.920 --> 00:23:18.030
Then put the chain on the closest gear.

00:23:15.550 --> 00:23:18.340
Now put it on the closest, 
most accessible gear.

00:23:18.910 --> 00:23:19.820
There.

00:23:19.820 --> 00:23:22.290
Okay, now slowly turn the pedals.

00:23:22.620 --> 00:23:25.290
You did it.

00:23:23.010 --> 00:23:25.290
And that's it.

00:23:25.290 --> 00:23:29.890
Since it's so easy to fix, just do it slowly 
and properly like I just showed you,

00:23:29.300 --> 00:23:34.930
<b>Next Time
How to Perform Maintenance</b>

00:23:29.890 --> 00:23:31.840
and you'll have fixed it in no time.

00:23:31.840 --> 00:23:33.220
Try it out for yourselves.

00:23:33.220 --> 00:23:33.990
Okay.

00:23:33.220 --> 00:23:34.930
Got it.

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>Next Time
What Can I Do?</b>
